ttps://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T18:47:55-08:00","id":1527026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526718-hate-for-gaia-bring-back-the-lupines-in-vtm?p=1527021#post1527021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's never gonna work and is a terrible idea because when you try that, your players will expect to see W:TA and feel cheated when it's not there.<br /> There's a description for the attempts to keep all the game lines separate: a bad idea.<br /> They DONT fit together, you're absolutely right but they're close enough for Gamemaster work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm. Are you sure about that? I've been doing it for decades and people don't mind. They're here to play the advertised game, not a mashup.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T19:22:27-08:00","id":1527028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526718-hate-for-gaia-bring-back-the-lupines-in-vtm?p=1527026#post1527026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Erm. Are you sure about that? I've been doing it for decades and people don't mind. They're here to play the advertised game, not a mashup.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, my players hate it and I hate it when I play so there's that. They expect crossover and prefer me to make it more palatable between gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T19:26:38-08:00","id":1527029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526718-hate-for-gaia-bring-back-the-lupines-in-vtm?p=1527021#post1527021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's never gonna work and is a terrible idea because when you try that, your players will expect to see W:TA and feel cheated when it's not there.<br /> <br /> There's a description for the attempts to keep all the game lines separate: a bad idea.<br /> <br /> They DONT fit together, you're absolutely right but they're close enough for Gamemaster work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as an ardent fan and defender of a big and messy crossover World of Darkness, I don't think that needs to operate as a default assumption. It's probably important to discuss with your play-group, find out what expectations people have for the game and such, but what option is best is ultimately a product of that conversation. Obviously there's no good to come from trying to force a WoD crossover from a Storyteller that is uninterested or unable to tell that kind of story. And a group of new players who were drawn in very specifically by (insert game-line) may not be best served by a game that forces them to deal with the Rashomon-style mess of bringing the full complexity of *every* game-line into the narrative.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526718-hate-for-gaia-bring-back-the-lupines-in-vtm?p=1527022#post1527022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From an anti-materiel rifle on a ballistic trajectory over the horizon, aimed by long-range sensory Gifts?</div> </div> </div> </div>This was what popped into my brain as soon as you mentioned a nasty bullet-Talen being a more straightforward option. It's something that's been in the back of my brain for a little bit, and I think this is the final nudge I need to actually make a thread about it. So I'm going to edit in a link to said thread after I finish setting it up.<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes\">Link</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Submariner93</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526718-hate-for-gaia-bring-back-the-lupines-in-vtm?p=1526975#post1526975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you all for the insightful answers. I see werewolves as a toolkit: a supernatural antagonist, a boogeyman, a dip into nature and animism, etc... so everything you have written can be useful. I never thought about the fact that maybe it's ok for the character (and for the player) to not understand at all what is going on, or try to understand gifts, auspices and spirit world stuff (unless explicitly being important for a character). Maybe in that case another vampire NPC could be helpful in giving some filtered explanations.<br /> <br /> I will definitely check the hunter manual and Crimson Thaw for inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Especially if the role you envision for the Garou is that of &quot;the boogeyman,&quot; having most of what's actually going on not be comprehensible to the characters (or players) is not only acceptable, but a good thing. You shouldn't be looking for the chance to use it to gank someone, but you can add some genuine horror by having them dealing with a threat that does not follow rules that they can understand.<br /> <br /> Using vampire NPCs for filtered explanations is definitely a good idea. And it's important to remember that, from the perspective of a crossover-style World of Darkness, even those filtered perspectives are going to be <b>immensely</b> limited outside of quite exceptional circumstances. Many previous versions of WoD games had a special Knowledge stat called &quot;Lore&quot; that characters could acquire, with different versions for the various types of supernatural beings, and being able to know pretty much *anything* about the specific details of others splats was predominantly limited to N/PCs with that specific Trait. And even then, you'd have to have 4 or 5 dots to come close to the amount of knowledge that the typical player gets just out of reading one of the core rulebooks.<br /> <br /> (I realized writing this paragraph that I don't think you've specified an edition. Lore still exists in Mage 20, but I can't recall if it comes up in the other 20A lines. And other editions are mostly outside my knowledge.)<br /> <br /> Even a Werewolf character probably shouldn't know everything that you can find in just the core rulebook for WtA, so your average Vampire is not going to have a clue about how any of the Garou's various abilities work. That's the realm of hardcore specialists and Methuselahs, who can be expected to have learned more simply by virtue of the quantity of time they have available to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":".  Added Link mentioned before 12-18-2023, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}